<title>BRAZIL: Ships loading/unloading commodities - Brazil ports.</title>
<headline>Ships loading/unloading commodities - Brazil ports.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following ships were loading, unloading or announced on May 7 at the Brazilian ports of Santos, Recife and Maceio, port authorities said.</p>
<p>Where announced, time of arrival is given by day and month.</p>
<p>Quantities are in tonnes.</p>
<p> SANTOS							 AGENT</p>
<p> Bebedouro	     ldg    13,100 FCOJ	     Cargill</p>
<p> Ouro do Brasil	ldg    14,000 FCOJ</p>
<p> Lamyra		  ldg    54,000 soybeans</p>
<p> Flag Diamond	  ldg    55,000 soybeans	 Cargill</p>
<p> Novi		    dsg    24,210 wheat	    Itamaraty</p>
<p> Solon		   dsg    23,100 wheat</p>
<p> Waiting to dock/announced				AGENT</p>
<p> Southway		to dsg 15,750 wheat	    Dickinson</p>
<p> Leonid Sobolyev     07/05  20,000 wheat	    Tropical</p>
<p> Glory Hope	    to ld  53,000 soybeans	 T. Carriers</p>
<p> Brilliance	    07/05  40,000 soymeal	  Cargill</p>
<p> Bagesta		 10/05  60,000 soybeans	 Itamaraty</p>
<p> Mister Michael	11/05  43,000 soybeans	 Multicargo</p>
<p> RECIFE							 AGENT</p>
<p> Moonlight I	   ldg     6,000 bagged sugar   Pelagos</p>
<p> Petersfield	   dsg     3,525 barley	   Start</p>
<p> Norsul Ipu	    dsg    26,220 wheat	    Fertimport</p>
<p> La Rioja		dsg     9,179 corn	     Agemar</p>
<p>Waiting to dock/expected</p>
<p>None</p>
<p> MACEIO							 AGENT</p>
<p> Pericles		ldg    12,000 bulk sugar     Williams</p>
<p> Semena		  ldg    20,532 bulk sugar</p>
<p>Waiting to dock/expected</p>
<p> Heracleto Dantas    14/05   5,500 wheat</p>
<p> Boss		    15/05  12,000 wheat</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
